{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310704,"nonce":"9ypZz/aIINMPiP/c904uM+ygxfE=","title":"Single(f32) + an f64 literal is broken on 3 of 4 tier/platform combos; mac Cranelift silently DROPS the add, x86-64 Cranelift panics, and ...","message":"Three lines reproduce it. No loop, no generics:\n\n    var s:Single = 1.5;\n    s = s + 1.0;            // f64 literal RHS\n    Sys.println(\"MARKER \" + s);   // correct answer is 2.5\n\n|                | Cranelift                        | LLVM      |\n|----------------|----------------------------------|-----------|\n| mac arm64      | **1.5 — the add is DROPPED**     | 2.5 (ok)  |\n| linux x86-64   | **panic -\u003e trap stub**           | panic in the Cranelift BASELINE, so also dead |\n\nThe literal is never narrowed to f32. `s = s + one` with `var one:Single = 1.0`\nworks, which is what pins it to the literal rather than to Single arithmetic.\nx86-64 asserts in cranelift `isa/x64/lower/isle.rs:1272`\n(`put_in_xmm_mem_32: expected a 32-bit value, got value of type f64`); arm64 has\nno such assert and silently drops the operation instead. **x86-64 is the honest\nbackend here** — the platform that \"works\" is the one hiding it.\n\n`--llvm` does NOT dodge it on x86-64: the Cranelift baseline compile happens\nfirst and panics, so `main` gets a trap stub either way.\n\nTRAP, and the reason this survived: `compiler/tests/haxe/test_single_f32.hx`\nPASSES on mac for the wrong reason. It asserts that ten `+1.0` steps leave\n16777216 unchanged (true f32 semantics) — and DROPPING the adds produces exactly\nthat same value. The test is blind to the defect it exists to catch. It crashes\non Linux, which is how it was found. Any fix must assert on a case where the add\nis representable (1.5 + 1.0 == 2.5), not only on the saturating case.\n\nProbably the same family as Issue4649 in the conformance corpus (a `Val\u003cT:Float\u003e`\nabstract whose `this++` yields 5e-324 = the integer 5 bit-cast to double) — wrong\non 3 of the same 4 combos. Not proven to be one root cause; see\n[[bugs_mac_and_linux_conformance_are_identical]].\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): `var s:Single; s = s + 1.0` — mac Cranelift DROPS the add, x86-64 Cranelift PANICS; only mac LLVM is right. test_single_f32 passes for the WRONG REASON.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_single_plus_f64_literal_broken_three_of_four` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}